9. Use of any prescription medications, over-the-counter medications, traditional Chinese patent medicines, herbal remedies, vitamin dietary supplements, or health products within 4 weeks prior to signing the informed consent form;
10. Habitual intake of or consumption of excessive amounts of xanthine or caffeine-containing foods, beverages, or other substances that may affect drug absorption, distribution, metabolism, or excretion within 1 month prior to screening or within 72 hours before using the investigational drug. Examples include: coffee (more than 1100 mL per day), tea (more than 2200 mL per day), cola (more than 2200 mL per day), energy drinks (more than 1100 mL per day), chocolate (more than 510 g per day);
